{
  "fps": 30,
  "durationInFrames": 3426,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "from": 0,
      "duration": 390,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Across UX Labs studies, maps had a sixty-eight percent click rate.",
          "file": "hook-0.wav",
          "start": 0.7,
          "seconds": 4.137416666666667,
          "from": 21,
          "duration": 124
        },
        {
          "text": "Travelers plan on maps. They check what's close, and whether a day is even possible.",
          "file": "hook-1.wav",
          "start": 5.187416666666667,
          "seconds": 5.004083333333333,
          "from": 156,
          "duration": 150
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "title",
      "from": 390,
      "duration": 132,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "from": 522,
      "duration": 431,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "On Bing, planning a trip meant switching between apps and sites for hotels, flights, activities and transit.",
          "file": "problem-0.wav",
          "start": 18,
          "seconds": 6.598875,
          "from": 540,
          "duration": 198
        },
        {
          "text": "There was no way to narrow the map to what mattered, and little help deciding where to go at all.",
          "file": "problem-1.wav",
          "start": 24.948874999999997,
          "seconds": 5.231083333333333,
          "from": 748,
          "duration": 157
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "insight",
      "from": 953,
      "duration": 165,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Travelers don't plan in lists.",
          "file": "insight-0.wav",
          "start": 32.266666666666666,
          "seconds": 1.7214583333333333,
          "from": 968,
          "duration": 52
        },
        {
          "text": "They plan in places.",
          "file": "insight-1.wav",
          "start": 34.338125,
          "seconds": 1.32325,
          "from": 1030,
          "duration": 40
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision1",
      "from": 1118,
      "duration": 466,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Many travelers start without a destination, so the map starts there too.",
          "file": "decision1-0.wav",
          "start": 38.06666666666666,
          "seconds": 4.21475,
          "from": 1142,
          "duration": 126
        },
        {
          "text": "It groups places by continent, offers trips nearby priced from where you're browsing, and themes like beaches or adventure narrow the field.",
          "file": "decision1-1.wav",
          "start": 42.63141666666667,
          "seconds": 8.771666666666667,
          "from": 1279,
          "duration": 263
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision2",
      "from": 1584,
      "duration": 454,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Then I brought every travel vertical onto a single map.",
          "file": "decision2-0.wav",
          "start": 53.599999999999994,
          "seconds": 3.342,
          "from": 1608,
          "duration": 100
        },
        {
          "text": "One search covers destinations, hotels and attractions, and the map pins all of them, so a hotel's distance from the sights shows at a glance.",
          "file": "decision2-1.wav",
          "start": 57.291999999999994,
          "seconds": 9.227916666666667,
          "from": 1719,
          "duration": 277
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision3",
      "from": 2038,
      "duration": 435,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "But a map with every pin is as hard to read as a long list.",
          "file": "decision3-0.wav",
          "start": 68.73333333333333,
          "seconds": 3.5864166666666666,
          "from": 2062,
          "duration": 108
        },
        {
          "text": "So filters narrow it to attractions, stays or restaurants, where a heat map shows demand, and transit shows how to get around.",
          "file": "decision3-1.wav",
          "start": 72.66975000000001,
          "seconds": 8.175166666666666,
          "from": 2180,
          "duration": 245
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "result",
      "from": 2473,
      "duration": 619,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I explored the map from mild to wild. The mild ideas gave engineering something to build early, and the wild ones showed where it could go.",
          "file": "result-0.wav",
          "start": 83.23333333333333,
          "seconds": 8.910333333333334,
          "from": 2497,
          "duration": 267
        },
        {
          "text": "Then I tested the concepts with users, prioritized an MVP with product and engineering, and delivered its key modules.",
          "file": "result-1.wav",
          "start": 92.49366666666667,
          "seconds": 8.182125,
          "from": 2775,
          "duration": 245
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "takeaway",
      "from": 3092,
      "duration": 184,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Design without constraints first, then let the team decide what ships.",
          "file": "takeaway-0.wav",
          "start": 103.56666666666666,
          "seconds": 4.24325,
          "from": 3107,
          "duration": 127
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "end",
      "from": 3276,
      "duration": 150,
      "lines": []
    }
  ]
}
